== Notable people ==
{{Main|List of people from Ise Prefecture}}
* {{nihongo|Kuroda Tetsuya|黒田 徹也}} (born 1952) — Master swordsmith and designated [[Living National Treasure]], credited with reviving the Ichijoudani forging tradition
* {{nihongo|Hoshino Ayame|星野 あやめ}} (born 1968) — Historian and author of the definitive ''Kinzō Incident: A Reappraisal'' (1998), which challenged the traditional narrative of Ii Naotaka's culpability
* {{nihongo|Fujimoto Kōsuke|藤本 浩介}} (born 1974) — Tea master and cultivator who developed the {{nihongo|Echizen Gold|越前金|Echizen-kin}} tea cultivar, now the second-most-planted variety in Ise
* {{nihongo|Nakagawa Chiaki|中川 千秋}} (born 1981) — Award-winning filmmaker whose historical drama ''The Letter of Blood'' (2015) depicted the final hours of the Siege of Ichijōdani
* {{nihongo|Matsumura Haruka|松村 遥}} (born 1988) — Olympic archer and descendant of the Ii clan retainers, who won silver at the 2012 Adonian Games
* {{nihongo|Takahashi Ren|高橋 蓮}} (born 1944) — Forester and conservationist who established the Echizen Range sustainable management protocols
* {{nihongo|Inoue Masako|井上 雅子}} (born 1956) — Herbalist and director of the Eiheiji Institute of Traditional Medicine, pioneer of integrative pharmacological research
* {{nihongo|Morimoto Shinji|森本 真司}} (born 1963) — Architect who designed the [[Ichijōdani Castle Reconstruction Museum]], awarded the [[Sanese Architecture Prize]] in 2012
* {{nihongo|Yamashita Aoi|山下 葵}} (born 1995) — Professional {{nihongo|shogi|将棋}} player, the youngest ever to achieve 8-dan ranking
* {{nihongo|Sakurai Daisuke|桜井 大輔}} (born 1979) — Lacquerware artist whose contemporary interpretations of Ise-shikki have been exhibited at the [[Okami Museum of Modern Art]]

